Description: Oaxaca graphics and session layer (metapackage)
 Everything between the base system and the desktop: Mesa (OpenGL, EGL,
 Vulkan and VA-API drivers for Intel, AMD and virtual GPUs), the Hyprland
 compositor with Xwayland for X11 applications, uwsm to run the compositor
 as a systemd user session, the SDDM display manager with Qt's Wayland
 platform plugin for its greeter, and the desktop portals (the Hyprland
 backend for screen sharing and screenshots, the GTK backend for file
 dialogs), Quickshell 0.3.2 or newer (the Qt/QML toolkit the desktop
 shell runs on; the archive's 0.3.0 predates fixes to the session lock),
 and GNOME Keyring as the secret store (the Secret Service
 that browsers and other desktop applications keep credentials in),
 with its PAM module so that the login password unlocks the keyring and
 a password change follows. The NVIDIA install path comes through
 oaxaca-nvidia.
 .
 This package also configures SDDM: its greeter runs on Wayland under a
 Hyprland instance with a minimal configuration, so no X server and no
 second compositor are needed for the login screen.
